  "success": [
    "Both explicit R7 inputs pass safe-path, race, length, SHA-256, schema, repository, revision, tree, source-manifest, document, producer, and toolchain validation.",
    "A bounded wire framing pass rejects amplification, malformed fields, illegal wire types, excess recursion, and count or length overflow before generated protobuf decode.",
    "Recursive unknown fields, duplicate singular values, non-canonical varints or field order, and canonical re-encoding drift fail before graph construction.",
    "Only UTF-8 Rust documents with valid UTF-8 byte ranges and exact committed source hashes can become in-repository compiler facts.",
    "Compiler symbol identities remain stable across document, occurrence, relationship, and scheduling permutations.",
    "RESOLVES_TO and REFERENCES require unique source and lexical-owner bindings; IMPLEMENTS and TYPE_DEFINITION require their explicit SCIP flags.",
    "Syntax and compiler evidence are both retained on disagreement; precedence never hides a conflict or incomplete coverage.",
    "External and generated symbols remain explicit unbound compiler assertions rather than committed source or runtime declarations.",
    "Absolute roots, raw arguments, embedded text, documentation, signatures, diagnostics, environment values, and privacy canaries do not reach public artifacts.",
    "No CALLS or runtime relationship is emitted and call/macro limitations remain exact coverage gaps.",
    "Publication, restart, corruption, crash, and sweep retain the immutable R6 semantics without migration.",
    "Every invocation without both R7 selector inputs remains byte-identical through R6."
  ],
